  <p><code>dd</code> came in after <code>ee</code> because I noticed dashboard tweaks were getting tangled with training code edits. Generic Claude would "improve the dashboard" by adding a new metric AND editing the training loop to emit it AND restarting the learner. The lane separation forces clean contracts: dashboard consumes metrics; producers expose them. (Aside: this <code>dd</code> is not the same <code>dd</code> writing this article's layout — same nickname, different repo, different crew. Convergent naming.)</p>

  <p><code>dd</code> owns <code>src/bot/dashboard.py</code> plus future frontend assets plus <code>drafts/dd/</code>. Read-only access to all of training, mod, fleet, and eval code.</p>

